From f17c3eb29d63266da7f7d1874751467f25b7de37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Gilbert <1travisgilbert@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:21:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] fix(fork): build the v0.7.3 rebase against the Theorem
 Zed source

Upstream v0.7.3 moves to gpui-pre 0.3.9 and adds an optional GPUI Fast
backend. The fork keeps every GPUI family crate on the one pinned
Travis-Gilbert/zed revision (6d4d9075), so:

- GPUI Fast is not carried. gpui-fast-linux needs `oo7 ^0.6`, which cannot
  resolve beside the Zed fork's `oo7 =0.6.0-alpha`, and a second engine
  would be a second GPUI type identity. The gpui-fast dependencies and
  features leave every manifest; the `cfg(feature = "gpui-fast")` sources
  stay byte-identical and inert, declared through check-cfg.
- The Zed source has no `IndentAdjustment`, so `LineWrapper::wrap_line`
  takes two arguments again. Its default behaviour is the same-indent wrap
  upstream asks for.
- The Zed source has no separate background and glyph passes on
  `TextLayout`. `Inline` keeps #3439's order (backgrounds, selection,
  glyphs) by painting the run backgrounds itself and shaping the text
  without them, so the shaped text paints only glyphs over the selection.
- `FrameTiming` has no refresh interval, signal time or phases, so the fps
  sampler's test frames omit them; criterion stays at 0.5, the version the
  Zed source's bench-support links.
- The Zed GPUI macros expand to bare `gpui::` paths. Since #3306,
  `gpui_kit::gpui` is the Kit itself, so a crate that names `gpui`
  directly and glob-imports the Kit is ambiguous (E0659). The Kit-only
  consumers (the story, tig, the recipes tests and the exports test) use
  the one line #3306 documents, `extern crate gpui_kit as gpui;`, instead
  of a direct `gpui` dependency.
- Three files the text merge left unformatted are formatted again.
